{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Never want my hand cut off
[Bb]Never want a hacking cough
Never need a cliffside push
Never turn my brain to mush
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Always give me what I lack
Always take the best parts back
Always recognize your fate
Always just a moment late
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Left is where I always turn
Left is how I'm forced to learn
Left the room my walking takes
Left to alone with my mistakes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Up against a person who
Up til now I never knew
Up from hell the answer blew
Up and down it's up to you.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[Db]Drop [Eb]me off the chinese [F]wall
and peel my fingers off the rim
I come unglued while in mid-air and land to reform
Limb by limb
[F]limb by limb by [Bb]limb by limb by [F]limb by limb by[Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[F](And I am [Bb]taken far away) [F]Lingering slowly and [Bb]melting away
(And I am taken far away) Tossed with the salad and baled with the hay
(And I am taken far away) Pooling like water that drips from above
(And I am taken far away) Trampled by lambs and pecked by the dove
{end_of_verse}

